  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Life Saving Emergency Support in NES  Der-Ez-Zor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project aims to provide life-saving WASH assistance through sustainable and emergency interventions&#xa0;to vulnerable populations in Ar-Raqqa and Deir ez Zor governorates by Concern Worldwide (CW). The project addresses critical water access gaps and contributes to the prevention of waterborne (WBD) and vector-borne diseases (VBD) through the&#xa0;Rehabilitation of water supply systems.ltbrgtConcern will rehabilitate five water stations, two in Ar-Raqqa and three in Deir ez Zor governorates which have already been identified in coordination with local authorities and the WASH Cluster. The rehabilitation works will aim to&#xa0;provide&#xa0;safe and sustained water supply by replacing or repairing pumps, pipes, valves, chlorination and sedimentation systems, storage tanks, and conducting related civil and electrical works aiming to improve water access by providing reliable and safe water in conflict-affected communities and to reduce dependency on&#xa0;costly emergency trucking.ltbrgtAll proposed interventions have been designed in alignment with the WASH Cluster strategy and have been discussed and agreed upon at the sub-national level to ensure complementarity and avoid duplication. The project targets highly vulnerable communities with limited or no access to safe water&#xa0;and prioritises areas at high risk of disease outbreaks.ltbrgtThis project contributes to both humanitarian response and early recovery, supporting resilience and reducing long-term dependence on emergency support.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
